v0u|n|A round or spherical body, solid or hollow; a body whose surface is in every part equidistant from the center; a ball; a sphere. ; Anything which is nearly spherical or globular in shape; as, the globe of the eye; the globe of a lamp. ; The earth; the terraqueous ball; -- usually preceded by the definite article. ; A round model of the world; a spherical representation of the earth or heavens; as, a terrestrial or celestial globe; -- called also artificial globe. ; A body of troops, or of men or animals, drawn up in a circle; -- a military formation used by the Romans, answering to the modern infantry square.	a:181j,84,3;36v,66,3;1vqz,49,5;vu4,47,3;vs8,29,2;89s,28,2;nyu,23,3;16i4,19,6;1imv,16,3;28qm,16,3;1vhw,11,3;27h1,9,2;on3,7,1~16i4,19,6;1vqz,49,5;36v,66,3;181j,84,3;1vhw,11,3;vu4,47,3;nyu,23,3;28qm,16,3;1imv,16,3;27h1,9,2;vs8,29,2;89s,28,2;on3,7,1	v:1wsu,71,15;1r2j,60,5;s30,37,2~1wsu,71,15;1r2j,60,5;s30,37,2	V:wxf,61,1;1ldl,38,2;40c,28,4~40c,28,4;1ldl,38,2;wxf,61,1	n:8p6,85,3;1wsu,58,6;mss,39,4;vu4,31,1;s30,27,1;297r,26,3;1om8,23,6~1om8,23,6;1wsu,58,6;mss,39,4;8p6,85,3;297r,26,3;s30,27,1;vu4,31,1	N:wxf,71,2;201o,56,1;207j,53,6;mss,39,4;ze8,38,13;36z,33,1;9ud,16,5;14cl,12,6;16io,6,1~ze8,38,13;207j,53,6;14cl,12,6;9ud,16,5;mss,39,4;wxf,71,2;36z,33,1;201o,56,1;16io,6,1
